    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "Mathematics feels like a bridge between abstract ideas and practical problem-solving—something my father taught me through simple arithmetic while baking bread. It’s not intimidating but requires patience, especially since I never pursued formal education beyond primary school. My interest lies in its logical structure, though I often struggle with complex formulas due to limited exposure.",
